Z||000003||2M4 Dale||10-09-2001||11:46 AM||||Nightfier and dirty bird are one in the same car !!! My 1987 Econo Coupe. I'm glad you liked it......it's nice to see someone pick my car as a favorite out of so many great Fiero pics !!!<P>It is a 87 coupe with a black prismatique paint job, polished tech wheels with Goodyear rubber. the drive train is just a stock Duke with a 5 speed...but she runs GREAT !!! My ride also has a Jenson AM/FM/Cassette with a Jenson 6 disc changer...a 35 watt Pheonix Saphire Gold amp pushing a 8" Power Accoustic sub in a custom RSM center console box. Plus Kenwood 4X10's and Kenwood Excellon 4X6" speakers in the factory locations.<P>Future mods include the instalation of a "built" 88 2.8L V6 and all poly bushings and Mr Mikes leather seat covers.||||reg||7
Z||000004||x-thumpr-x||10-09-2001||01:37 PM||||Devish belongs to a GTA Fiero Club member. She runs "Race Tech Fiero Shop" here in Toronto. I'm not too sure but she might have a user handle here in PFF. Maybe "Devlish" since she has a thing for that name. Any GTA member would know why. LOL<P> <A HREF="http://www.thefieroshop.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefieroshop.com/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Old Lar||10-09-2001||02:39 PM||||Coupe w flames and DevilishM are two of Old Lar's photos in the gallery.  The coupe was some one visiting the FOCOA Nationals at Columbus Ohio a few years ago.  Owner ?? I thought it was a very nice looking painted flame job on a coupe too.<P>The DevilishM photo was taken at Carlisle in the spring when Miriammee came in from Canada with Joe Trentadue ("The Fiero Shop"), maybe two years ago.  The last I knew they removed the hood for safe keeping, as the car didn't have that hood at the Louisville show in 2000. That car graphic is one of the best I've seen, and the car won Best of Show at Columbus in 1999.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fix||10-09-2001||04:39 PM||||Dale, that is a nice looking 87 coupe.  In fact I have one that looks exactly like it.  I don't have a digital camera, so in the past when someone has asked me what my car looks like, I have pointed them to the picture of your car and told them that it's pretty much the same thing.  I never knew who the car belonged to before, but rest assured that mine won't look the same for much longer.  It's in the process of getting a V8 and a few body mods.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>"If it doesn't scare you, it's not fast enough."||||reg||14
